{title: Softly and Tenderly Jesus Is Calling}
{artist: Will L. Thompson}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 6/8}
{meta: tune THOMPSON - Will L. Thompson (1880)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1880, tune 1880: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Softly and tenderly [C]Jesus is [G]calling,
Calling for you and for [D]me;
[G]See, on the portals He's [C]waiting and [G]watching,
Watching for [D]you and for [G]me.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Come home, [G]come home, [D]ye who are weary, come [G]home;
[G]Earnestly, tenderly, [C]Jesus is [G]calling,
Calling, O [D]sinner, come [G]home!
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Why should we tarry when [C]Jesus is [G]pleading,
Pleading for you and for [D]me?
[G]Why should we linger and [C]heed not His [G]mercies,
Mercies for [D]you and for [G]me?
{end_of_verse}
